Package: sfgpu
Title: Explicit CPU, CUDA, and Metal Distances for Projected Points
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Egor", "Kotov", email = "kotov.egor@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Computes dense Euclidean distance matrices for Cartesian two-column
    coordinates and projected 'sf' POINT geometries. A portable double-precision
    CPU backend is always available; optional NVIDIA CUDA and Apple Metal
    backends must be requested explicitly at build time and at each call.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Suggests: sf, units, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: C++17; optional NVIDIA CUDA toolkit for --enable-cuda;
    Apple Metal SDK for --enable-metal
